      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "A  recording studio charges musicians an initial fee of $$80$ to record an album. The studio also charges an additional $$50$ per hour.\n\nWhat expression gives the cost, in dollars, of recording an album,  in terms of the number of hours $h$ used?",
      "worked_solution": "The fixed fee for recording an album is $$80.$ Hence,  $80$ should be a constant term.\n\nNow, if $h$ is the number of hours used to record an album, the cost  for $h$ hours of a recording must be $50h$ dollars.\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost, in dollars, of recording an album will be $50h+80.$",
